# One half of a pair with `.gitignore`, which says the same about itself.
#
# What belongs in both is anything a *build* must not see: dependencies, build
# output, git's own directory, and every `.env` (deploy.example.sh keeps its
# settings in .env.production; any .env.* holds APP_SECRET). What each file also
# carries on its own is fine — a name that matches at any depth belongs to
# `.gitignore`, which is about the tree rather than about a build context.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
server/data
